ersion you can  access the two structures search  interfaces from the top cam home page  and both interfaces support various  types of search including identity  search substructure superstructure  search and similarity search and  molecular formula search and you can  provide the input structure using the  pubchem compound ID or line notations  like smiles in cheese and indicates and  you can also draw the input structure  using the pubchem sketcher or upload a  file that contains the input structure  and pop cam is actively working on a new  interface that that will replace the two  existing interfaces so please stay tuned  another important topic to cover is a  structure clustering and structural  activity analysis or SAR analysis a  structure clustering is about grouping  compounds into small clusters according  to their structural similarities it is  helpful in classifying molecules  according to their structural  characteristics as an example these are  some anti-allergic agents from pubchem  they can be grouped into three major  clusters like dipeptides glucocorticoids  and antihistamines based on these a  clustering result you can expect that  the anti-allergic activities of these  compounds may come from three different  mechanisms of action and so our analysis  is about clustering compounds  and bio essay data simultaneously it is  useful for identifying structural  characteristics responsible for the bio  activity of molecules  unfortunately the structure clustering  and syrup analysis tools will be retired  by the end of this year but at the same  tasks can still be done using  third-party software after downloading  necessary data from pubchem last one is  automated data retrieval using a  computer code app upcam provides  multiple programmatic access routes  among them park rest is the simplest and  easiest to learn and use and it can be  used with popular programming languages  like Python so students can learn how to  automate data retrieval from pub